Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Figure. ",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 "Top-5 cosine nearest neighbours by decade. Any subset of ",
 StyleBox["deWords[]",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " can be passed to ",
 StyleBox["deNeighborTable",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 "."
}], "Caption",
 CellMargins->{{55, 55}, {2, 
  16}},ExpressionUUID->"d6fee7a9-0fbe-48be-bd46-679abea300e0"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Takeaway.  ",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 "Trajectories can be cross-checked against plain word lists. When the ",
 "neighbours of ",
 StyleBox["broadcast",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " go from ",
 StyleBox["sow, scatter",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " to ",
 StyleBox["radio, television",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 ", the drawn path is just reporting that shift."
}], "Text",
 CellFrame->{{3, 0}, {0, 0}},
 CellMargins->{{60, 60}, {8, 12}},
 CellFrameColor->RGBColor[0.35, 0.6, 0.4],
 FontSize->12,
 Background->RGBColor[
  0.93, 0.97, 0.93],ExpressionUUID->"fb5442a3-4eaf-4b9c-b72c-524cd65b1a73"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["7. Two statistical laws of semantic change", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"b82ea4ce-b255-4f3f-b0e8-4a9ad32472fd"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Hamilton, Leskovec & Jurafsky (2016) propose two regularities of semantic \
",
 "change. Both can be tested directly on the aligned embeddings, measured \
over the ",
 StyleBox["11332",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " dictionary content words present in every decade (function ",
 "words and archaic/foreign tokens removed via a stoplist and ",
 StyleBox["WordData",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 " membership). A word's ",
 StyleBox["rate of change",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " is the mean cosine distance ",
 "between its aligned vectors in consecutive decades; its ",
 StyleBox["frequency",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " is proxied by its mean rank, and its ",
 StyleBox["polysemy",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " by its number of WordNet senses. Re-deriving the laws independently is \
also a good ",
 "way to watch a confound masquerade as a result. (Statistics: ",
 StyleBox["deLawFacts[]",
  FontFamily->"Courier"],
 ".)"
}], "Text",
 CellMargins->{{50, 50}, {6, 
  6}},ExpressionUUID->"3aa011b8-7a61-4055-b59a-6408380c4ab5"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["The law of conformity \[Dash] holds", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"96cd3db5-3be6-471d-9206-d1c77193458a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["More frequent words change more slowly.",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " Change-rate falls steeply ",
 "with frequency (Spearman \[Rho] = ",
 "-0.94",
 ", slope ",
 "-0.12",
 " in log-rate). ",
 StyleBox["Why:",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " a high-frequency word is seen ",
 "in a huge range of contexts, so its vector is an average over many uses and \
is ",
 "statistically well-anchored. Part of the strength is also methodological \
\[Dash] rare ",
 "words are estimated from little data, so their vectors are noisier and ",
 StyleBox["look",
  FontSlant->Italic],
 " like they move more \[Dash] which is itself worth stating plainly."
}], "Text",
 CellMargins->{{50, 50}, {6, 
  6}},ExpressionUUID->"6d92a64a-4435-4055-81c4-aee8114e470a"],

